**Question:** Disable the CHECK on Medications.UnitCost, insert a bad row, then re-enable the CHECK WITH CHECK and see what happens.

```sql
ALTER TABLE healthcare.Medications NOCHECK CONSTRAINT CK_Medications_1;
INSERT INTO healthcare.Medications VALUES (999, N'Bad price drug', 'MED-99999', -1);

BEGIN TRY
    ALTER TABLE healthcare.Medications WITH CHECK CHECK CONSTRAINT CK_Medications_1;
    SELECT 'Re-enabled' AS Result;
END TRY
BEGIN CATCH
    SELECT ERROR_NUMBER() AS ErrorNo, ERROR_MESSAGE() AS Message;
END CATCH;
```

**How it works:** NOCHECK lets bad data in. Re-enabling WITH CHECK validates existing rows and fails on the bad one. Re-enabling without WITH CHECK leaves the constraint "not trusted", and the optimizer then ignores it.

**Expected result:** 1 row

| ErrorNo | Message |
|---|---|
